  "system": {
    "identifier": "grimnir-circle-of-the-devourer-primal-protection",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><b>Circle of the Devourer · уровень 3</b></p><p>The primal spirits exert their powers to protect you. If you are hit by an attack, you may use a Reaction to roll on the<br>Primal Protection table to determine a defensive effect.<br>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom Modifier, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p><hr><p><b>Автоматизация / ограничения:</b></p><ul><li>После определения результата активировать только выпавший эффект. С 14 уровня выбирать без 1d6, расход остаётся 1. Конец следующего хода и отталкивание — вручную.</li></ul><h3>Primal Protection Table</h3><p>Primal Protection<br>1d6<br>Effect<br>1–2<br>Protruding Spines. Jagged spines burst from<br>your body. Each creature within 5 feet of you<br>takes 2d4 plus your Wisdom modifier Piercing<br>damage and is pushed 5 feet away from you. The<br>spines then retract.<br>3–4<br>Bulbous Shell. Your skin hardens into a thick,<br>mottled shell. You gain a +3 bonus to AC until the<br>end of your next turn. If this increased AC would<br>cause the triggering attack to miss you, it does.<br>5<br>Abyssal Glare. Your eyes become glowing purple<br>orbs until the end of your next turn. Whenever<br>a creature deals damage to you, including the<br>triggering attack, it takes Psychic damage equal to<br>twice your Wisdom modifier.<br>6<br>Aberrant Flesh. Your flesh warps and knits itself<br>back together. You regain 2d4 plus your Wisdom<br>Modifier Hit Points immediately after taking the<br>triggering damage.<br></p>"
    },
